from c8e_base import *
LB(8,5,'Language work: adjectives, merged words, future time, silent letters, advice and an article','Language work for Claribel and the space story: adjectives, merged words, future time, silent letters','Words for a trip through space',
 "Sven and the crew of a spaceship nearly lose their pet canary Claribel. The language work of this science fiction story teaches us to choose precise adjectives, to build merged words, to talk about the future in seven ways, to pronounce silent letters, to ask for and give advice and to write an article.",
 [("Adjectives describe nouns, and the right adjective makes a picture. Match nagging with worry, narrow with path, vague with plan, sheepish with look, inexplicable with reason, sluggish with traffic, hushed with voices and delighted with expression.","nagging worry, narrow path, vague plan"),
  ("Nagging means constantly troubling, vague means not clear, inexplicable means impossible to explain, sluggish means slow-moving, hushed means very quiet, and sheepish means embarrassed because you did something silly.","meanings of the adjectives"),
  ("A merged word is made by combining parts of two words. Intercom comes from internal and communication, and brunch comes from breakfast and lunch. Others are motel from motor and hotel, smog from smoke and fog, sitcom from situation and comedy, vlog from video and log, spork from spoon and fork, and webinar from web and seminar.","merged words: motel, smog, sitcom, vlog, spork, webinar"),
  ("Verbs can talk about the future in several ways. Will is used for offers, promises, predictions and willingness, as in 'I will help you with your homework'.","will"),
  ("The simple present tense is used for the future when it is a fixed schedule: 'Our flight leaves at 10 a.m. tomorrow' and 'My school reopens on 3 January'.","simple present for timetables"),
  ("The present progressive tense is used for personal arrangements and fixed plans: 'We are moving into our new house next month' and 'I am visiting my grandparents'.","present progressive for plans"),
  ("Going to is used in an informal way for plans and for things we can see are about to happen: 'We are going to get a new motorbike soon'.","going to"),
  ("The future perfect, will have plus the third form of the verb, says that something will be finished by a certain time: 'The teacher will have completed the portions by next month'. The future progressive, will be plus -ing, says that something will be going on at a moment in the future: 'This time tomorrow I will be relaxing at home'.","will have + past participle; will be + -ing"),
  ("Sometimes, when we tell a story about the past, we need to mention something that was still in the future at that time. We say 'you were going to start a new business' and 'I arrived in a town where I would spend the rest of my life'. This is the future in the past.","future in the past: was going to, would"),
  ("Silent letters are written but not pronounced. In ballet the t is silent, in whistle the t is silent, in receipt the p is silent, in debris the s is silent, in pneumonia the p is silent, in almond the l is silent, in foreign the g is silent, in island the s is silent, in wreck the w is silent, in aisle the s is silent, in campaign the g is silent and in fasten the t is silent.","silent letters"),
  ("To ask for advice we say 'What should I do?' or 'How can I make sure...?' To give advice we say 'I feel you should...' or 'It is best to use...'. These polite phrases are useful for the solar system model and the Chandrayaan-3 quiz situations in the book.","asking and giving advice"),
  ("For the writing task, make a web of the uses of the internet, then write an article titled 'The Importance of Internet'. Give a heading, your name, a general introduction in paragraph one, the uses and examples in paragraph two, and a thoughtful closing comment or quote in paragraph three.","article: heading, name, three paragraphs"),
  ("For the listening task you hear Monika and Toby, a Martian stranded on Earth, talking about food, school and how he sees. Read the statements first, then tick the correct ones and cross the wrong ones while you listen, and listen again to fill the blanks with the exact words.","listening task")],
 ("Join the words 'smoke' and 'fog' into one merged word, and write a sentence about a plan using 'going to'.",
  [("Smoke and fog make the merged word smog.","A merged word combines parts of two words."),
   ("A sentence: 'We are going to visit the science museum next Saturday.'","Going to is used for plans and informal speech.")]),
 ("Explain two different ways of talking about the future in English with one example each.",
  ["will is used for offers, promises and predictions","the simple present is used for timetables and fixed schedules","the present progressive is used for personal plans","a correct example for each way chosen"],
  ["Using will for every future plan","Using the present progressive for a timetable that nobody planned personally"]),
 ["Adjectives such as nagging, vague and sheepish describe nouns exactly.","Merged words: intercom, brunch, motel, smog, sitcom, vlog, webinar.","Future forms: will, simple present, present progressive, going to, will have, will be, and the future in the past.","Silent letters: ballet, whistle, receipt, debris, pneumonia, almond, foreign, island, wreck, aisle, campaign, fasten.","An article has a heading, a byline and three paragraphs."],
 [mcq("v5a-1",1,"Which adjective best completes 'a ___ path'?","narrow",[("hushed","Hushed describes a quiet voice, not a path."),("delighted","Delighted describes a happy person.")],"A path can be narrow."),
  mcq("v5a-2",1,"The merged word 'smog' comes from","smoke and fog",[("small and fog","Small is not a part of smog."),("smell and fog","Smell is not a part of smog.")],"Smoke plus fog gives smog."),
  mcq("v5a-3",1,"'Our flight ___ at 10 a.m. tomorrow.' Choose the best verb form for a timetable.","leaves",[("will be leaving","This is a future progressive, not the usual timetable form."),("left","This is the past tense.")],"The simple present is used for fixed schedules."),
  mcq("v5a-4",1,"In which word is the letter p silent?","receipt",[("pencil","The p is pronounced in pencil."),("paper","The p is pronounced in paper.")],"Receipt is pronounced re-seet."),
  mcq("v5a-5",1,"'I ___ you with your homework after dinner.' The best answer for an offer is","will help",[("am helping","This shows a fixed arrangement, not an offer."),("helped","This is the past tense.")],"Will is used for offers."),
  mcq("v5a-6",2,"'We ___ into our new house next month.' The best form for a personal plan is","are moving",[("move","The simple present suits a timetable, not a personal plan."),("moved","This is the past tense.")],"The present progressive is used for fixed personal plans."),
  mcq("v5a-7",2,"Which sentence uses the future perfect?","The teacher will have completed the portions by next month.",[("The teacher will complete the portions.","This is the simple future."),("The teacher is completing the portions.","This is the present progressive.")],"Will have plus past participle shows something finished by a time in the future."),
  mcq("v5a-8",2,"'This time tomorrow I ___ at home.' Which form shows something in progress in the future?","will be relaxing",[("will relax","This does not stress that it will be going on."),("relaxed","This is the past tense.")],"Will be plus -ing shows an action in progress."),
  mcq("v5a-9",2,"Which word is a merged word?","webinar",[("website","This is a compound word of two whole words."),("sandwich","This is a normal word.")],"Webinar combines web and seminar."),
  mcq("v5a-10",2,"'Last time I saw you, you ___ start a new business.' Choose the future in the past.","were going to",[("are going to","This is the present."),("will","This is not in the past.")],"Were going to is the future in the past."),
  mcq("v5a-11",3,"Which phrase is used for giving advice?","I feel you should check the measurements.",[("What should I do?","This asks for advice."),("How can I make sure?","This also asks for advice.")],"I feel you should gives advice."),
  mcq("v5a-12",3,"How many paragraphs does the article on 'The Importance of Internet' have, as given in the book's points?","three",[("two","The points give an introduction, uses and a closing comment."),("five","The points do not ask for five.")],"Introduction, uses, closing comment.")])
